WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.900
In 1498, Michelangelo began carving
a single block of Carrara marble.

2
00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:07.910
He was about 24.

3
00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:12.790
It is the only work he ever signed,
on a sash across Mary's chest.

4
00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:16.440
Today it stands in St
Peter's Basilica in Rome.

5
00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:20.080
Mary holds the dead body
of Jesus across her lap.

6
00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:22.640
A mother holds her dead son.

7
00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:25.680
So why do Catholics
find hope, not despair,

8
00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:27.190
in that statue?

9
00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:31.030
In this mission, you'll study
the statue detail by detail:

10
00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:33.840
its pyramid shape and her lowered eyes.

11
00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:38.670
Then you'll find out why Catholic churches
and homes are full of statues at all.

12
00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:43.550
Your mission: find out why Catholics
see hope in a statue of grief.
